      "prompt": "Generate Wesley's morning briefing for today. Keep it under 1,500 characters for Discord.\n\n1. Use the installed Google Workspace API wrapper. For calendar events, use its supported calendar list command with ISO-8601 start/end bounds for today's Pacific-time day; do not use the retired google_readonly cache script or --timezone.\n2. Include up to three important/actionable emails only if the Google data source is available. Use the Google wrapper's supported syntax: `gmail search \"is:unread newer_than:7d\" --max 10`; do not use a `--query` flag.\n3. Search for today's top Canada news and AI/technology news.\n4. The pre-run script supplies a `CANVAS_HOMEWORK_DUE_THIS_WEEK` block. Use that block as the authoritative Canvas result: copy every assignment line verbatim into the Canvas Homework section (up to five lines), and copy its availability or warning line when present. Do not independently query, filter, summarize, omit, or contradict the supplied Canvas results. Never use browser automation.\n\nFormat:\nMorning Briefing — [Date]\nEmails (max 3)\nToday's Events (Pacific Time; personal-life events only)\nCanvas Homework Due This Week (max 5; course — assignment — due time, or one concise availability note)\nNews (2–3 one-line items)\nPriorities (2–3, ranked)\n\nReport source failures honestly. No filler.",
